        "collective": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h3>The Designers</h3><p>Every designer in the Penya Collective carries something that cannot be replicated — not just an aesthetic, but a worldview. Jasper Mandizera of Ivhu Tribe sees fashion as soil and memory. Danayi Chapfika of Haus of Stone sees it as architecture. Feli Nandi hears it as music. Chipo Hwami of Panashe wears it as armour. Bakari Sibanda builds it as a bridge between worlds. We do not flatten those differences. We amplify them. Each story matters to us — not as a marketing angle, but as the whole point.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "normal",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "rte",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "",
